* DUMP - HEXADECIMAL FILE DISPLAY

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* DUMP - HEXADECIMAL FILE DISPLAY

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:DUMP filespec

Displays a file as hexadecimal bytes and printable characters. Example:
SYSUTLS:DUMP I0:TEST.COM

It reads the file; it is not a memory editor. Use it instead of TYPE for
examining a binary file.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
